WEBVTT

00:00:06.547 --> 00:00:08.216
( tongue flapping )

00:00:10.843 --> 00:00:12.053
( laughs )

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.057
But the food
they longed for the most

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.725
was the cocoa bean.

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.560
( laughs )

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:21.229
( snorts )

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.397
An Oompa-Loompa was lucky

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:25.775
if he found three or four
cocoa beans a year.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:29.237
But oh, how they craved them.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.949
All they’d ever think about
was cocoa beans.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:36.118
( playing tribal music )

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:40.081
The cocoa bean
happens to be the thing

00:00:40.164 --> 00:00:43.000
from which chocolate is made,
so I told the chief...

00:00:47.755 --> 00:00:49.674
( whoops )

00:00:49.757 --> 00:00:51.425
( ululating )

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.844
( honking )

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:05.857
They are such
wonderful workers.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.233
I feel I must
warn you, though,

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:09.318
they are rather mischievous.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.237
Always making jokes.

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:13.447
Augustus, mein child,
that is not

00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:15.324
a good thing you do.

00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:19.662
Hey, little boy,
my chocolate

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:20.997
must be untouched

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.456
by human hands.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.292
( screams )

00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:26.127
( gasping )

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.381
He’ll drown!

00:01:31.465 --> 00:01:33.843
He can’t swim!

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.553
Save him!

00:01:35.636 --> 00:01:36.596
( gasping )

00:01:36.637 --> 00:01:38.264
Augustus, no!

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:48.065
Augustus!

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.660
Augustus, get out!

00:01:59.702 --> 00:02:04.457
( screaming fades, gets louder
as Augustus circles )

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:12.673
( gasping )

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.428
There he goes.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.180
( screams )

00:02:19.263 --> 00:02:21.098
Call the fire brigade!

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:23.184
It’s a wonder
how that pipe is big enough.

00:02:24.101 --> 00:02:25.603
CHARLIE:
It isn’t big enough.

00:02:25.686 --> 00:02:26.687
He’s slowing down.

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:28.105
He’s going to stick.

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:29.357
( screams )

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.942
I think he has.

00:02:31.025 --> 00:02:33.027
( grunting )

00:02:34.362 --> 00:02:36.280
He’s backed the whole pipe.

00:02:38.699 --> 00:02:41.285
Look. The Oompa-Loompas.

00:02:45.039 --> 00:02:46.415
What are they doing?

00:02:48.876 --> 00:02:51.212
Why, I believe they’re going
to treat us to a little song.

00:02:51.253 --> 00:02:53.214
It is quite a special
occasion, of course.

00:02:53.255 --> 00:02:55.675
They haven’t had a fresh
audience in many a moon.

00:02:55.716 --> 00:02:58.219
( upbeat melody playing )

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:07.353
( horns join in,
Oompa-Loompas chant in rhythm )

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:18.072
♪ Augustus Gloop,
Augustus Gloop ♪

00:03:18.155 --> 00:03:20.908
♪ The great big
greedy nincompoop ♪

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.244
♪ Augustus Gloop,
so big and vile ♪

00:03:23.285 --> 00:03:25.746
♪ So greedy, foul
and infantile ♪

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:28.416
♪ "Come on," we cry,
"the time is right ♪

00:03:28.457 --> 00:03:31.127
♪ To send him shooting
up the pipe" ♪

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.587
♪ But don’t, dear
children, be alarmed ♪

00:03:33.671 --> 00:03:36.298
♪ Augustus Gloop
will not be harmed ♪

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.260
♪ Augustus Gloop
will not be harmed... ♪

00:03:48.144 --> 00:03:50.396
♪ ♪

00:03:57.778 --> 00:04:00.072
♪ Ah, ah, ah ♪

00:04:00.114 --> 00:04:05.119
♪ Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah! ♪

00:04:05.202 --> 00:04:10.166
( heavy rhythm playing )

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.334
♪ Although, of course,
we must admit ♪

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.628
♪ He will be altered
quite a bit ♪

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.965
♪ Slowly wheels go round
and round ♪

00:04:18.007 --> 00:04:20.217
♪ And cogs begin to grind
and pound ♪

00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:23.429
♪ This greedy brute,
this louse who’s here ♪

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.600
♪ Is loved
by people everywhere ♪

00:04:27.641 --> 00:04:30.644
♪ For who can hate
or bear a grudge ♪

00:04:30.728 --> 00:04:37.318
♪ Against a luscious square
of fudge? ♪

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.535
No!

00:04:55.836 --> 00:04:59.173
( song fades to an end )

00:04:59.256 --> 00:05:01.759
Bravo! Well done!

00:05:01.842 --> 00:05:04.428
Aren’t they delightful?
Aren’t they charming?

00:05:04.512 --> 00:05:06.847
I do say that all seemed
rather rehearsed.

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:08.057
Like they knew

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.100
what was going to happen.

00:05:09.183 --> 00:05:11.685
Oh, poppycock.

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:16.023
Where is my son?

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:17.608
Where does that pipe go to?

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.362
That pipe--
it just so happens to lead

00:05:21.403 --> 00:05:23.197
directly to the
room where I make

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.532
the most delicious kind

00:05:24.573 --> 00:05:26.450
of strawberry-flavored
chocolate-coated fudge.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.869
Then he will be made
into strawberry-flavored

00:05:28.953 --> 00:05:30.204
chocolate-coated fudge?

00:05:30.287 --> 00:05:31.539
They’ll be selling him

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.207
by the pound all over the world?

00:05:34.041 --> 00:05:35.793
No. I wouldn’t allow it.

00:05:35.876 --> 00:05:37.002
The taste would be terrible.

00:05:37.044 --> 00:05:38.212
Can you imagine

00:05:38.295 --> 00:05:40.381
Augustus-flavored
chocolate-coated Gloop?

00:05:40.422 --> 00:05:42.842
Ew! No one would buy it.

00:05:45.219 --> 00:05:47.721
( ululating )

00:05:50.766 --> 00:05:54.937
I want you to take Mrs. Gloop
up to the fudge room, okay?

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.564
Help her find her son.

00:05:56.605 --> 00:05:58.649
And take a long stick
and start

00:05:58.732 --> 00:06:02.486
poking around in the big
chocolate mixing barrel, okay?

00:06:11.412 --> 00:06:13.539
( Mrs. Gloop groans )

00:06:19.003 --> 00:06:20.045
Mr. Wonka?

00:06:20.087 --> 00:06:21.255
Huh?

00:06:21.297 --> 00:06:22.590
Why would Augustus’ name
already be

00:06:22.673 --> 00:06:25.134
in the Oompa-Loompa song
unless they...?

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:26.927
Improvisation is a parlor trick.

00:06:27.011 --> 00:06:28.262
Anyone can do it.

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:30.723
You, little girl,
say something.

00:06:30.764 --> 00:06:31.765
Anything.

00:06:31.807 --> 00:06:32.933
Chewing gum.

00:06:32.975 --> 00:06:34.351
( sing-songy ):
Chewing gum is really gross;

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:36.395
chewing gum I hate the most.

00:06:36.437 --> 00:06:37.688
See? Exactly the same.

00:06:38.355 --> 00:06:39.440
No, it isn’t.

00:06:39.481 --> 00:06:42.443
Uh, you really
shouldn’t mumble,

00:06:42.526 --> 00:06:45.279
because I can’t understand
a word you’re saying.

00:06:46.363 --> 00:06:50.576
Now... on with the tour.

00:06:52.369 --> 00:06:54.622
Are the Oompa-Loompas
really joking, Grandpa?

00:06:54.663 --> 00:06:56.749
Of course they’re joking.

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:59.960
That boy will be fine.

00:07:09.845 --> 00:07:12.264
( deep, ominous melody playing )

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:24.652
♪ ♪

